1
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:05,087
"It's a '57-facet
round brilliant pink."

2
00:00:06,088 --> 00:00:07,632
"3.82 carat."

3
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:11,093
It's gorgeous.

4
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:13,721
"It's one of the most exquisite diamonds
we have."

5
00:00:14,597 --> 00:00:18,684
It's such an unusual color.
It must be really expensive.

6
00:00:19,852 --> 00:00:22,313
It's on the higher end
of our line, but...

7
00:00:23,564 --> 00:00:25,858
Unique and very special.

8
00:00:28,402 --> 00:00:29,862
Should we do it?

9
00:00:34,116 --> 00:00:35,952
- We'll take it.
- Excellent.

10
00:00:36,577 --> 00:00:40,456
I wish you every happiness
Mr. Cho, Mrs. Cho.

11
00:00:40,706 --> 00:00:42,750
Honey, I love it.

12
00:00:44,293 --> 00:00:45,586
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

13
00:00:45,711 --> 00:00:47,046
Sweetie.

14
00:01:01,143 --> 00:01:02,186
Here you go.

15
00:01:02,728 --> 00:01:04,272
She's a beaut.

16
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:07,024
- You all right?
- Yeah, just a little, uh...

17
00:01:08,609 --> 00:01:10,987
- A little tickle in my throat.
- You sound like you're getting a cold.

18
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:13,114
- You should see a doctor.
- Oh, I don't need a doctor.

19
00:01:13,614 --> 00:01:15,241
- Frauds in white coats.
- Whatever.

20
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:17,994
Just don't sneeze near me.
The last thing I need is a cold.

21
00:01:18,327 --> 00:01:19,704
- Will do.
- We got a live one.

22
00:01:20,037 --> 00:01:22,331
There's no question this diamond's part
of the stolen cache.

23
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:25,835
- Carat, cut, color all match.
- Let's go get the bad jeweler.

24
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:32,800
Why don't you go back
to my place, jump into bed?

25
00:01:32,925 --> 00:01:34,468
I'll come tuck you in
as soon as we're done.

26
00:01:34,635 --> 00:01:36,095
No, I'd rather be here with you.

27
00:01:44,854 --> 00:01:49,400
- Is something wrong?
- F.B.I. the engagement's off.

28
00:02:02,745 --> 00:02:06,373
"Six weeks ago, two security guards
were killed outside of Fort Worth."

29
00:02:06,498 --> 00:02:08,584
"They were transporting half a million
dollars worth of diamonds."

30
00:02:08,834 --> 00:02:10,252
What does that have to do with me?

31
00:02:10,628 --> 00:02:13,589
The diamond you sold out
was part of the stolen shipment.

32
00:02:14,423 --> 00:02:15,466
No. No, wait.

33
00:02:16,008 --> 00:02:17,051
Six weeks ago?

34
00:02:18,177 --> 00:02:20,804
I was out of the country.
In Barcelona.

35
00:02:21,263 --> 00:02:23,140
- Wren will tell you.
- It's true. He was.

36
00:02:23,515 --> 00:02:25,517
We don't suspect you killed
the man yourself.

37
00:02:25,684 --> 00:02:28,228
- Not with those hands, you certainly didn't.
- But you planned it.

38
00:02:28,395 --> 00:02:29,855
Or got the diamond from
the people who did.

39
00:02:30,105 --> 00:02:33,025
I purchase the diamond I sold you
legitimately two weeks ago.

40
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:35,235
I bought many gems that day
from several dealers.

41
00:02:35,402 --> 00:02:37,237
We'll need their names.
And the receipts.

42
00:02:37,446 --> 00:02:38,489
I'm sorry. The receipts?

43
00:02:38,614 --> 00:02:41,450
Little pieces of paper they give you
when you buy something.

44
00:02:41,575 --> 00:02:44,370
Yes, yes, of course. I just don't know
what I can put my hands on.

45
00:02:44,578 --> 00:02:46,997
{\an8}We have a new office manager,
and everything is in disarray.

46
00:02:47,164 --> 00:02:50,626
{\an8}Isn't it amazing how easy it is
to spot an illicit couple?

47
00:02:51,001 --> 00:02:53,295
{\an8}And they always think
they're fooling everyone.

48
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:57,508
- It's just... I just think it's amazing.
- I assure you, that's...

49
00:02:57,633 --> 00:03:03,013
{\an8}Don't even try to defend yourself here.
Look at you, with your petite manicure

50
00:03:03,138 --> 00:03:05,349
{\an8}and your pocket square,
your spray tan.

51
00:03:05,474 --> 00:03:08,227
Everything screams mid-life crisis
impending divorce

52
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,980
and sweet Wren's charming blush
tells us the rest of the sordid tale.

53
00:03:12,106 --> 00:03:14,149
{\an8}If you're planning on getting
a divorce, Mr. Joubert

54
00:03:14,274 --> 00:03:15,943
{\an8}you'd want to hide
your assets.

55
00:03:16,193 --> 00:03:17,778
Is that why you don't have
any receipts?

56
00:03:18,028 --> 00:03:20,447
{\an8}I'm not getting a divorce.
That's ridiculous.

57
00:03:20,989 --> 00:03:22,032
I love my wife.

58
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,118
- She speaks.
- Wren.

59
00:03:24,535 --> 00:03:25,577
Take that back.

60
00:03:25,869 --> 00:03:27,287
We are gonna need those receipts.

61
00:03:29,790 --> 00:03:33,335
{\an8}Word of advice... he cheated on her
he's probably gonna cheat on you

62
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:36,588
{\an8}and I know that probably seems
very difficult to believe right now

63
00:03:36,714 --> 00:03:38,841
{\an8}but it's the way of the world, kid.

64
00:03:50,686 --> 00:03:52,312
- Morning, Agent.
- Vega.

65
00:03:54,606 --> 00:03:57,151
{\an8}- How'd it go at the jewelry store?
- It went okay.

66
00:03:59,236 --> 00:04:00,821
{\an8}- Make any arrests?
- Nope.

67
00:04:02,448 --> 00:04:05,576
- Got anything useful?
- Not sure yet.

68
00:04:08,454 --> 00:04:10,789
Sir, I know you're angry

69
00:04:11,874 --> 00:04:15,085
{\an8}and I just wanna say again,
I am sorry for lying to you.

70
00:04:15,544 --> 00:04:18,213
{\an8}Abbott did not give me clearance to go
on the mission

71
00:04:18,589 --> 00:04:19,840
{\an8}and yet I said he had.

72
00:04:20,215 --> 00:04:21,383
It's inexcusable.

73
00:04:22,426 --> 00:04:24,845
{\an8}Let me know what I have to do
to make it up to you and I'll do it.

74
00:04:25,971 --> 00:04:27,014
Okay.

75
00:04:30,309 --> 00:04:31,518
{\an8}"Are you sure
you're all right?"

76
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:34,438
{\an8}Oh, yeah. Just a little
lemon and honey for the throat

77
00:04:34,563 --> 00:04:36,190
- and I'll be right as rain.
- You look pale.

78
00:04:36,482 --> 00:04:37,524
Thank you.

79
00:04:40,068 --> 00:04:42,237
{\an8}Hey. Did you get the receipts
from the jeweler?

80
00:04:42,362 --> 00:04:44,490
- Wylie's working on that right now.
- Okay, good.

81
00:04:44,615 --> 00:04:46,992
Has your wife heard back from
the commerce department yet?

82
00:04:47,284 --> 00:04:49,495
No, not yet, and she better
hear soon.

83
00:04:49,787 --> 00:04:52,247
She's been waiting for months
wound tighter than a piano wire.

84
00:04:52,414 --> 00:04:54,208
- Tell her I said good luck.
- Me, too.

85
00:04:54,625 --> 00:04:55,667
You look pale.

86
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:57,753
Told you.

87
00:04:58,045 --> 00:04:59,880
{\an8}Wylie, where are we
with the jeweler?

88
00:05:00,172 --> 00:05:02,049
{\an8}Joubert jewelers has been
a family-owned business

89
00:05:02,174 --> 00:05:04,009
for three generations...
no legal troubles.

90
00:05:04,134 --> 00:05:05,886
- And what about Joubert's alibi?
- It checks out.

91
00:05:06,011 --> 00:05:07,846
He was out of the country
until three weeks ago.

92
00:05:08,263 --> 00:05:11,099
{\an8}And, the story that he bought
the diamond legitimately?

93
00:05:11,308 --> 00:05:12,476
It also checks out.

94
00:05:12,643 --> 00:05:15,771
His receipts show that someone
named Josef Rosales sold him

95
00:05:15,896 --> 00:05:18,106
$50,000 worth of diamonds
2 weeks ago

96
00:05:18,232 --> 00:05:19,942
{\an8}including several
Australian pinks.

97
00:05:20,484 --> 00:05:23,445
{\an8}- Who's Rosales?
- He's a vendor at a traveling gem show.

98
00:05:24,863 --> 00:05:28,575
It... it's a, uh, gem market
that travels from city to city.

99
00:05:29,201 --> 00:05:31,036
{\an8}Vendors buy gems
in large quantities

100
00:05:31,161 --> 00:05:33,580
{\an8}and then sell them at the show
to retailers like Joubert.

101
00:05:33,789 --> 00:05:36,208
- And where's this gem show now?
- Houston through the end of the week.

102
00:05:36,959 --> 00:05:39,169
Well, why don't you head over
and talk to Rosales?

103
00:05:39,336 --> 00:05:41,380
We'll hang back here
and work on the receipts

104
00:05:41,505 --> 00:05:43,966
- see who else Joubert bought from.
- Sure.

105
00:05:45,092 --> 00:05:48,428
{\an8}Cho, why don't you, take Vega?

106
00:05:50,347 --> 00:05:51,390
I'd rather take Lisbon.

107
00:05:51,640 --> 00:05:55,894
{\an8}Take Vega. She told me
what happened and apologized.

108
00:05:56,353 --> 00:05:58,689
What she did was wrong,
but she's young.

109
00:05:59,398 --> 00:06:00,858
And reformable, I think.

110
00:06:02,818 --> 00:06:03,944
Vega, let's go.

111
00:06:04,945 --> 00:06:06,363
Ye... yes, sir, right away.

112
00:06:12,744 --> 00:06:16,081
Also on display is our blue
and purple Tanzanite

113
00:06:16,206 --> 00:06:17,749
from Mount Kilimanjaro.

114
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,794
"This is a highly prized gem
due to its scarcity."

115
00:06:21,128 --> 00:06:24,464
"Another color-changing gem
is the Alexandrite from Russia's..."

116
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:27,968
- You ever interrogate a suspect?
- I've done practice interrogations.

117
00:06:28,218 --> 00:06:30,637
Then you haven't.
Follow my lead.

118
00:06:30,971 --> 00:06:32,764
If you're not sure if you
should ask a question, don't.

119
00:06:33,432 --> 00:06:34,892
Try not to lie to anyone.

120
00:06:35,183 --> 00:06:37,853
- "We have several black opals in the back."
- Got it.

121
00:06:38,186 --> 00:06:41,189
"These have a fire in them, trust me."

122
00:06:41,732 --> 00:06:43,442
"Don't go by their name."

123
00:06:43,609 --> 00:06:47,321
"And finally, sapphire,
the gem that..."

124
00:06:52,242 --> 00:06:54,953
Our full cooperation.
Just let me know.

125
00:06:55,495 --> 00:06:59,875
- Is something the matter?
- I'm Agent Cho. This is Agent Vega. F.B.I.

126
00:07:00,334 --> 00:07:01,501
Kirk Upton.

127
00:07:03,295 --> 00:07:05,422
- I saw your badge.
- Yeah, we're looking for Josef Rosales.

128
00:07:05,756 --> 00:07:09,301
Josef. Yeah, his booth's right over there.
Is he in trouble?

129
00:07:10,052 --> 00:07:12,054
- How well do you know him?
- Not really well.

130
00:07:12,179 --> 00:07:14,264
I haven't really been
with the show that long.

131
00:07:14,848 --> 00:07:16,642
Agents Cho, Vega.

132
00:07:17,017 --> 00:07:19,728
Elon Bell, head of security.
I was told you'd be coming. Welcome.

133
00:07:20,228 --> 00:07:22,898
- You think stolen gems are being sold?
- Is that why you're here?

134
00:07:23,023 --> 00:07:26,068
Mr. Upton, give us some space,
if you don't mind.

135
00:07:26,818 --> 00:07:29,237
Yeah. Sure. Sorry.

136
00:07:30,322 --> 00:07:32,074
If someone's using the market
to sell stolen goods

137
00:07:32,199 --> 00:07:33,867
that's of significant concern.

138
00:07:34,326 --> 00:07:35,786
My bosses want me to help
any way I can.

139
00:07:36,078 --> 00:07:38,664
We need to speak to some of your vendors
starting with Josef Rosales.

140
00:07:38,789 --> 00:07:40,916
- Absolutely. This way.
- Thanks.

141
00:07:46,421 --> 00:07:48,632
- "Hey."
- Hey. Lena. Hey, what's up?

142
00:07:48,924 --> 00:07:51,677
I was gonna call, but I wanted
to tell you in person.

143
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:54,012
You got the call.

144
00:07:54,346 --> 00:07:56,515
Bob Ackerman texted me
half an hour ago.

145
00:07:56,765 --> 00:07:58,684
You are looking at
the next undersecretary

146
00:07:58,809 --> 00:08:00,727
for the Department
of Commerce, baby!

147
00:08:01,186 --> 00:08:05,482
Yes! Yes! Oh, baby,
I knew it. I knew it.

148
00:08:05,941 --> 00:08:09,319
- Well, I'm glad you did, 'cause I didn't.
- No, no, no. See, you deserve this.

149
00:08:09,861 --> 00:08:10,904
You earned this.

150
00:08:11,279 --> 00:08:12,698
Because you're Wonder Woman.

151
00:08:14,741 --> 00:08:16,952
We got to celebrate.
We got to celebrate big, too.

152
00:08:17,077 --> 00:08:18,120
It's not a done deal yet.

153
00:08:18,245 --> 00:08:19,997
I have to be confirmed,
and that could take months.

154
00:08:20,122 --> 00:08:22,708
I don't care. I don't care.
You know what this is?

155
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:25,168
This is your chance
to make a difference.

156
00:08:25,293 --> 00:08:27,045
I know. It's...

157
00:08:28,088 --> 00:08:30,882
- I can't tell you how much I've wanted this.
- Oh, I know.

158
00:08:32,592 --> 00:08:35,595
Ackerman wants to meet for drinks tonight
and talk about the vetting process...

159
00:08:35,804 --> 00:08:37,848
- around 7:00?
- Absolutely.

160
00:08:38,557 --> 00:08:39,599
Great.

161
00:08:40,851 --> 00:08:41,935
Hey, Lena.

162
00:08:45,731 --> 00:08:46,982
You're there, baby.

163
00:08:48,859 --> 00:08:49,901
We're there.

164
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:56,616
- See you tonight.
- Yeah.

165
00:09:00,495 --> 00:09:03,373
- Yes!
- Yes, I sold diamonds to Jacques Joubert.

166
00:09:04,124 --> 00:09:07,044
He's a long-standing customer.
He purchases from me every year.

167
00:09:07,502 --> 00:09:09,046
And this year you sold him
stolen diamonds.

168
00:09:09,171 --> 00:09:11,381
- You think I'm stupid?
- Maybe. I don't know you yet.

169
00:09:11,715 --> 00:09:14,801
You know what? Go.
Take your little F.B.I. badges...

170
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:28,356
I suggested he calm down.

171
00:09:30,692 --> 00:09:32,486
Even if I wanted
to do something as stupid

172
00:09:32,611 --> 00:09:34,571
as pass stolen gems,
it would be impossible.

173
00:09:34,946 --> 00:09:35,989
Why is that?

174
00:09:36,114 --> 00:09:37,657
The gems are registered.
They are accounted for.

175
00:09:37,824 --> 00:09:38,950
How do you register a gem?

176
00:09:39,159 --> 00:09:42,162
Every gem has a serial number
saying when and where it was mined

177
00:09:42,370 --> 00:09:43,830
where and by whom
it was cut.

178
00:09:44,039 --> 00:09:45,999
Every gem I sold Joubert
had that number.

179
00:09:46,374 --> 00:09:48,251
If he had one that was stolen,
I don't know where he got it

180
00:09:48,376 --> 00:09:50,295
- but it wasn't from me.
- We need to look at your records.

181
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:51,755
- I have customers.
- Not until you're done with us.

182
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,715
Secure the area.
I'll be right there.

183
00:09:54,841 --> 00:09:56,885
Agents, can you check
something out with me?

184
00:09:57,219 --> 00:09:59,262
"Very special gems
being featured."

185
00:10:01,473 --> 00:10:03,850
"Somebody... We were
just coming around the corner."

186
00:10:15,403 --> 00:10:18,323
It's that guy who approached us. Upton.

187
00:10:26,703 --> 00:10:28,789
"Kirk Upton... 31 years old"

188
00:10:28,914 --> 00:10:31,959
San Antonio native,
recently divorced, two kids.

189
00:10:32,209 --> 00:10:34,128
- Any arrests?
- Uh, yes.

190
00:10:34,253 --> 00:10:35,629
Two misdemeanors and a felony

191
00:10:35,754 --> 00:10:38,841
"which didn't stick, none of it violent
all more than ten years ago."

192
00:10:39,341 --> 00:10:40,425
What's he been doing lately?

193
00:10:41,593 --> 00:10:45,180
Trying various moneymaking schemes
it looks like... none of them lasted.

194
00:10:45,556 --> 00:10:47,558
Then how is Upton's murder
connected with the gem heist?

195
00:10:47,766 --> 00:10:48,809
We don't know

196
00:10:48,934 --> 00:10:51,145
but he did not sell Joubert
that pink diamond.

197
00:10:51,270 --> 00:10:53,063
And he didn't have any
of the stolen gems in his booth.

198
00:10:53,230 --> 00:10:54,565
"Of course he didn't
have any on him."

199
00:10:54,857 --> 00:10:56,692
- He must have had a partner.
- "Why?"

200
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,652
"Because the gem heist
was engineered by a pro"

201
00:10:58,777 --> 00:11:00,654
not someone looking
for career counseling.

202
00:11:01,029 --> 00:11:03,699
Upton probably panicked
when he saw Cho and Vega

203
00:11:04,032 --> 00:11:06,910
told his partner to confess or run.
Boom.

204
00:11:07,161 --> 00:11:08,245
Who's the partner?

205
00:11:08,495 --> 00:11:10,747
Well, let's take a look
at Upton's associates.

206
00:11:11,081 --> 00:11:13,750
Lisbon, why don't you talk
to the ex-wife? Cho...

207
00:11:13,876 --> 00:11:15,752
"Why don't you and Vega
talk to anyone and everyone"

208
00:11:15,878 --> 00:11:17,796
"who came in contact
with Upton?"

209
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,299
Wylie, why don't you tap
into the security cameras

210
00:11:20,424 --> 00:11:21,466
at the convention center?

211
00:11:21,592 --> 00:11:25,095
See if you can find any footage
of Upton's movements before he died.

212
00:11:25,596 --> 00:11:26,972
- Jane...
- Yeah?

213
00:11:28,348 --> 00:11:31,185
- Go home.
- What, and miss all the fun?

214
00:11:33,896 --> 00:11:34,938
Poor Kirk.

215
00:11:36,607 --> 00:11:38,358
Good guy, basically.

216
00:11:38,734 --> 00:11:40,527
Just could never figure out
what he wanted to do.

217
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:43,447
{\an8}There was a new scheme
every month.

218
00:11:44,573 --> 00:11:46,408
{\an8}Eventually I had to get out
of the marriage.

219
00:11:46,533 --> 00:11:48,785
There's only so many fresh starts
you can take.

220
00:11:49,411 --> 00:11:50,871
What was his money situation?

221
00:11:52,748 --> 00:11:54,750
Kirk was in a motorcycle
accident last year.

222
00:11:55,334 --> 00:11:56,960
Doctors' bills?
Forget it.

223
00:11:57,502 --> 00:11:59,963
Plus, our boy Pauly
is special needs.

224
00:12:00,631 --> 00:12:01,798
Kirk was paying for his tutor.

225
00:12:02,132 --> 00:12:03,967
Is that why he got into
the gem business?

226
00:12:05,552 --> 00:12:08,430
He said some of those guys
make up to $100,000 a city

227
00:12:08,555 --> 00:12:12,226
once they get going
but he never saw that kind of money.

228
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:17,940
Records show that Kirk has two
misdemeanor convictions and an arrest?

229
00:12:18,232 --> 00:12:21,610
He hung with some bad guys
when he was younger.

230
00:12:22,194 --> 00:12:25,072
But be involved in a gem heist?

231
00:12:25,864 --> 00:12:27,366
Kirk just wanted to be a dad.

232
00:12:28,659 --> 00:12:30,744
Did he ever mention any friends
from the gem show?

233
00:12:31,787 --> 00:12:33,664
Someone named Lake...

234
00:12:33,956 --> 00:12:37,084
No. Pond. Walker Pond.

235
00:12:38,210 --> 00:12:39,461
This whole thing just kills me.

236
00:12:40,629 --> 00:12:42,339
Any idea who could have done this
to him, Mr. Pond?

237
00:12:42,631 --> 00:12:45,509
No. No, God, no.
Kirk's a...

238
00:12:47,469 --> 00:12:48,679
Kirk was a sweet kid.

239
00:12:49,513 --> 00:12:50,555
People liked him.

240
00:12:51,139 --> 00:12:52,182
You worked with him?

241
00:12:54,601 --> 00:12:55,978
I tried to help him.

242
00:12:57,229 --> 00:12:59,398
Kirk's, uh...
He was always amped up

243
00:12:59,898 --> 00:13:02,484
in a hurry.
I told him, "slow down."

244
00:13:03,277 --> 00:13:06,363
You know, "you got to build your business"
but, he didn't hear me.

245
00:13:06,863 --> 00:13:08,782
How does a gem seller go
about building his business?

246
00:13:09,032 --> 00:13:11,076
You've got to learn the trade.

247
00:13:11,785 --> 00:13:14,079
And that takes time.
Kirk wanted a shortcut.

248
00:13:14,454 --> 00:13:16,164
Anyone else Kirk was close to
at the show?

249
00:13:17,833 --> 00:13:20,502
I really don't know.
We only talked about business.

250
00:13:20,877 --> 00:13:21,920
Did you talk to him today?

251
00:13:22,129 --> 00:13:23,672
No. I got here late.

252
00:13:23,797 --> 00:13:26,133
Anyone you might have seen him
talking to, however briefly?

253
00:13:26,508 --> 00:13:30,429
Yes. I saw him a couple times
recently with Greta.

254
00:13:31,638 --> 00:13:33,056
Seemed to me like they were
having an argument.

255
00:13:33,181 --> 00:13:35,892
- And who's Greta?
- Greta Fortensky.

256
00:13:37,477 --> 00:13:41,732
She's the gem show appraiser.
She's been here... 15 or so years.

257
00:13:41,982 --> 00:13:44,776
- What's that?
- Vendors can't sell their gem

258
00:13:45,152 --> 00:13:48,196
without first having an appraiser
tell them what it's worth.

259
00:13:52,117 --> 00:13:54,202
Wylie. What's that?

260
00:13:54,703 --> 00:13:56,330
Security cam footage
from the gem show.

261
00:13:57,998 --> 00:13:59,916
- Live?
- No, it's from this morning.

262
00:14:00,042 --> 00:14:03,128
- I was tracking Kirk Upton.
- Oh. Well, uh...

263
00:14:04,713 --> 00:14:07,257
Possible to make it live?
I'd like to see what's going on there.

264
00:14:08,133 --> 00:14:09,176
Sure.

265
00:14:09,801 --> 00:14:10,844
Cool.

266
00:14:12,471 --> 00:14:15,182
I'm contracted by the gem show
as an independent appraiser

267
00:14:15,515 --> 00:14:17,642
which allows me to monitor
the show's integrity

268
00:14:17,768 --> 00:14:21,188
which stays sterling because
I keep the vendors honest.

269
00:14:22,064 --> 00:14:24,441
Their gems are priced
appropriately because of me.

270
00:14:26,693 --> 00:14:28,403
Bibby, don't do that.

271
00:14:29,154 --> 00:14:31,073
- Sorry, Mom.
- Come here.

272
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:35,285
My daughter Bibby
works with me.

273
00:14:36,203 --> 00:14:37,996
I learned how to appraise
gems from my own mother

274
00:14:38,372 --> 00:14:40,040
and Bibby will pick up
when I leave off.

275
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:41,583
It's nice to meet you.

276
00:14:42,292 --> 00:14:43,919
I understand you and Kirk
might have had an argument.

277
00:14:44,378 --> 00:14:46,755
No. He just thought I was
under-appraising his gems.

278
00:14:47,089 --> 00:14:48,840
That happens a lot
with younger vendors.

279
00:14:49,007 --> 00:14:52,219
- They dream of striking it rich fast.
- Which is not my problem.

280
00:14:52,511 --> 00:14:54,721
What happens when a vendor thinks
he's being under-appraised?

281
00:14:55,013 --> 00:14:56,640
We'll usually discuss it with them.

282
00:14:57,474 --> 00:14:58,600
And after we do...

283
00:14:59,684 --> 00:15:02,396
- my appraisal generally stands.
- Was Kirk Upton angry?

284
00:15:02,854 --> 00:15:06,024
Kirk was never angry.
He was just sad.

285
00:15:07,818 --> 00:15:09,194
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

286
00:15:11,947 --> 00:15:14,366
- Yeah?
- "Hey, Cho. Your fly's open."

287
00:15:17,244 --> 00:15:19,663
- "Jane, where are you?"
- The office. Where else?

288
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:25,127
- You're using the security cameras.
- Yeah, very good.

289
00:15:25,710 --> 00:15:29,214
- And, who is it that Vega's talking to?
- Greta Fortensky.

290
00:15:30,507 --> 00:15:32,008
She and her daughter
and appraisers.

291
00:15:32,342 --> 00:15:35,345
You think you could, show me the...
the woman Vega's talking to?

292
00:15:35,595 --> 00:15:36,888
Yeah, I think so.

293
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:38,849
She looks like a barrel of laughs.

294
00:15:39,141 --> 00:15:40,600
- Think she's the killer?
- I don't know yet.

295
00:15:41,059 --> 00:15:42,102
Well, looks like
she's got it in her.

296
00:15:42,269 --> 00:15:45,147
- "You think?"
- Sure. Look at that posture.

297
00:15:45,522 --> 00:15:48,733
I would bet money she has a riding crop
hidden in the closet somewhere.

298
00:15:49,192 --> 00:15:51,987
"And her daughter looks like
she'd like to give you an earful."

299
00:15:52,654 --> 00:15:53,697
Who are you talking to?

300
00:15:53,822 --> 00:15:55,115
- He's talking to Cho.
- Cho.

301
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:57,284
- Oh. May I?
- Oh. Yeah.

302
00:16:02,456 --> 00:16:04,833
Hey, Cho, hang on for a second.
I want you to hear this.

303
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:06,793
Put it on speaker.

304
00:16:08,253 --> 00:16:10,005
Wylie, what did you get
on Upton's movements?

305
00:16:10,422 --> 00:16:12,799
He left his booth after talking to
Cho and Vega

306
00:16:12,966 --> 00:16:14,468
according to the map...

307
00:16:14,843 --> 00:16:16,303
of the convention center

308
00:16:16,595 --> 00:16:19,723
the person he visited
was... Walker Pond.

309
00:16:20,015 --> 00:16:21,641
- Pond? You sure?
- Yeah. Why?

310
00:16:21,975 --> 00:16:23,518
Well, Pond told us he hadn't
talked to him today.

311
00:16:23,810 --> 00:16:26,062
Well, talk to him again
and see if his story stands.

312
00:16:26,813 --> 00:16:27,856
Yep.

313
00:16:29,608 --> 00:16:31,526
I'm, I'm just gonna...

314
00:16:33,570 --> 00:16:36,781
- Whoa, I'm getting the spins.
- Hey, why don't you go home?

315
00:16:37,157 --> 00:16:40,535
Yeah, just go home and
I'll get someone to drive you.

316
00:16:40,702 --> 00:16:43,413
Yeah, uh, that... that could be a good idea.
Hang on one second.

317
00:16:52,464 --> 00:16:53,507
Think he's running?

318
00:16:54,758 --> 00:16:55,800
Bell.

319
00:16:57,052 --> 00:16:58,386
We're looking for the vendor
who works that booth...

320
00:16:58,512 --> 00:17:00,430
- Walker Pond. You know him?
- Pond, sure.

321
00:17:00,555 --> 00:17:02,182
He packed up in a hurry
about 45 minutes ago.

322
00:17:02,307 --> 00:17:03,350
- Didn't say why.
- He's running.

323
00:17:03,725 --> 00:17:05,143
- Anything I can do to help?
- No, we got it.

324
00:17:05,769 --> 00:17:06,978
I'm gonna get Houston P.D.
to put out BOLO.

325
00:17:07,103 --> 00:17:08,438
Call Wylie, tell him to start tracking Pond.

326
00:17:08,563 --> 00:17:09,606
Yes, sir.

327
00:17:16,071 --> 00:17:17,113
Hey.

328
00:17:17,656 --> 00:17:19,950
Excuse me, sir? Sir?

329
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,745
We got a hit
off Pond's credit card.

330
00:17:23,912 --> 00:17:25,705
He bought gas at a station
outside Galveston.

331
00:17:25,872 --> 00:17:27,749
Galveston.
What was he doing there?

332
00:17:27,874 --> 00:17:30,418
Well, I checked, and Pond was
in the Air Force stationed at Galveston.

333
00:17:30,669 --> 00:17:31,711
Okay, so what did he do?

334
00:17:31,836 --> 00:17:33,838
He monitored planes
to and from South America.

335
00:17:34,047 --> 00:17:35,632
So you think that he's trying
to leave the country?

336
00:17:35,757 --> 00:17:36,800
I think he might be.

337
00:17:37,300 --> 00:17:38,969
There's a plane leaving
for the Yucatán at dawn.

338
00:17:39,094 --> 00:17:41,388
- Cho and Vega... they're in Houston, right?
- Yeah.

339
00:17:41,513 --> 00:17:44,391
Okay, so, uh, it's
a 45-minute drive to Galveston.

340
00:17:44,516 --> 00:17:47,352
Tell them to go to the airport
and sit and wait for that plane to leave

341
00:17:47,477 --> 00:17:49,854
just in case Pond arrives.

342
00:17:50,355 --> 00:17:51,523
- Okay.
- Okay.

343
00:18:04,286 --> 00:18:06,955
Lena, everyone
at Commerce is delighted.

344
00:18:07,247 --> 00:18:09,040
- You were our first choice.
- Well...

345
00:18:09,583 --> 00:18:11,710
I'm gonna choose
to believe that, Bob.

346
00:18:13,753 --> 00:18:15,046
All right, let's dig in.

347
00:18:16,047 --> 00:18:18,216
- Talk about getting you confirmed.
- Here we go.

348
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,093
Well, it's not you.

349
00:18:20,927 --> 00:18:23,888
The other side, well they just
want to stop the administration

350
00:18:24,014 --> 00:18:25,849
from accomplishing anything.

351
00:18:26,141 --> 00:18:27,892
They will use whatever
they can against you.

352
00:18:28,059 --> 00:18:29,352
- We're ready.
- Good.

353
00:18:29,519 --> 00:18:32,022
So Lena's résumé is impeccable.

354
00:18:32,772 --> 00:18:34,274
No problems there.

355
00:18:35,275 --> 00:18:37,110
We've got some people following
your paper trail.

356
00:18:37,569 --> 00:18:39,154
So far, so good.

357
00:18:40,655 --> 00:18:43,992
What about your personal lives?
I have to ask.

358
00:18:44,618 --> 00:18:46,369
- There's nothing to tell there, Bob.
- We met college.

359
00:18:46,494 --> 00:18:49,164
Married 17 years.
Never been happier.

360
00:18:49,331 --> 00:18:50,707
- All right.
- Well, okay.

361
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,043
What about you, Dennis?

362
00:18:54,210 --> 00:18:57,672
- What do you mean, what about him?
- Well, I'm not being confirmed here.

363
00:18:57,881 --> 00:18:59,382
Well, you're part of the package.

364
00:19:00,050 --> 00:19:04,471
You've had an exemplary career.
Some good talking points there.

365
00:19:05,972 --> 00:19:08,725
What can you tell me about
Rio Bravo station?

366
00:19:10,268 --> 00:19:13,229
- Wow, you have a file on me, too.
- Wouldn't be doing my job if I didn't.

367
00:19:13,647 --> 00:19:19,653
Right. Oh, well, Rio Bravo
was a joint task force... F.B.I., D.E.A.

368
00:19:20,195 --> 00:19:22,280
We were taking down the cartels
near the border.

369
00:19:22,906 --> 00:19:24,366
I was on the job about a year.

370
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:26,993
Did good work,
took down some bad guys.

371
00:19:27,369 --> 00:19:29,704
Dennis is really proud
of the work he did down there.

372
00:19:29,871 --> 00:19:31,790
Going after the cartels is tough.

373
00:19:32,874 --> 00:19:34,084
- It's tricky.
- Yeah.

374
00:19:34,292 --> 00:19:35,335
Dirty war.

375
00:19:36,336 --> 00:19:38,755
Hard to tell the criminals
from the cops sometimes.

376
00:19:40,256 --> 00:19:41,591
Anything to talk about?

377
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:46,846
- No.
- Nothing?

378
00:19:48,264 --> 00:19:50,850
Absolutely not.
We're all good here.

379
00:19:52,394 --> 00:19:53,436
All right.

380
00:19:53,561 --> 00:19:56,481
- Well, I'm starving.
- Me, too.

381
00:19:56,731 --> 00:19:58,274
- Let's eat.
- Thank you.

382
00:20:11,871 --> 00:20:14,207
Sir, I appreciate you inviting me
to work on this case with you.

383
00:20:14,499 --> 00:20:16,918
It wasn't my idea.
Abbott made me do it.

384
00:20:22,799 --> 00:20:25,635
I did apologize.
I understand what I did.

385
00:20:26,845 --> 00:20:28,263
It's about trust, okay?

386
00:20:29,055 --> 00:20:31,599
If we're gonna work together I need to be
able to trust you with my life.

387
00:20:32,809 --> 00:20:34,394
Now an apology is easy.
Trust is earned.

388
00:20:34,728 --> 00:20:36,020
Just tell me how.

389
00:20:38,148 --> 00:20:39,232
It's Pond.

390
00:20:47,449 --> 00:20:48,867
F.B.I.! Stop!

391
00:20:50,034 --> 00:20:52,245
Okay, okay. I didn't...

392
00:20:53,121 --> 00:20:54,414
- I didn't know it was you.
- What do you think you're doing?

393
00:20:54,831 --> 00:20:57,292
- I thought you were the other guy.
- Who? What other guy?

394
00:21:01,463 --> 00:21:03,715
- Do you know who that is?
- His name's Losa.

395
00:21:05,383 --> 00:21:08,344
Vega, stay here. Get Galveston P.D.
down here. I'm gonna go find this guy.

396
00:21:08,553 --> 00:21:09,596
Okay.

397
00:21:12,223 --> 00:21:13,266
No!

398
00:21:14,893 --> 00:21:15,935
Stop!

399
00:21:26,863 --> 00:21:27,947
Get your hands in the air!

400
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:30,700
I said get your hands
in the air.

401
00:21:31,201 --> 00:21:32,869
Off the ladder. Now.

402
00:21:36,998 --> 00:21:38,792
Okay. Stop.

403
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,920
Do not move. I said stop.
Stop... I will shoot...

404
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:27,137
Name's Uriel Losa.

405
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:29,014
He's muscle for
a Fort Worth loan shark.

406
00:22:29,389 --> 00:22:30,641
Pond apparently owes a lot.

407
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:32,559
Now Losa didn't know
we were F.B.I.

408
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:34,853
He thought we were there
to collect from Pond for someone else.

409
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:36,313
So why did he start shooting?

410
00:22:36,647 --> 00:22:38,273
Said he was just trying
to scare us away.

411
00:22:38,774 --> 00:22:40,901
- What happened there?
- Dealing with Pond. It's nothing.

412
00:22:41,068 --> 00:22:42,110
Minor sprain.

413
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:45,238
Job well done, you guys.
Both of you.

414
00:22:57,459 --> 00:23:00,253
Whatever you got to do
to me, go ahead.

415
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:02,297
It's my fault.

416
00:23:02,714 --> 00:23:03,882
Why is that, Mr. Pond?

417
00:23:04,883 --> 00:23:06,134
Because I got Kirk killed.

418
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:10,514
- How exactly did you do that?
- My business was off.

419
00:23:11,973 --> 00:23:13,850
So I borrowed money
from Losa's boss.

420
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:16,019
A lot of money.

421
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:17,729
And I was having trouble
paying it back.

422
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:19,606
Why not just throw him
a few rubies?

423
00:23:19,773 --> 00:23:22,109
Yeah. That's what
he wanted, too.

424
00:23:23,694 --> 00:23:24,820
I had to draw a line.

425
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:27,155
I owed him money.

426
00:23:27,823 --> 00:23:29,616
I wasn't gonna hand him
my career, too.

427
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:32,911
But he sent Losa after me.

428
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:36,748
- But he killed Kirk instead.
- Why would he do that?

429
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:40,794
I let Kirk borrow my hoodie
that morning.

430
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:43,380
You know, and we...

431
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:45,507
we had the same color,
same build...

432
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:48,051
So Losa must have thought
Kirk was me.

433
00:23:49,845 --> 00:23:51,930
And when Kirk went out
that fire exit, he killed him.

434
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:54,850
Why was Kirk using the fire exit
to begin with?

435
00:23:55,308 --> 00:23:56,351
To have a cigarette.

436
00:23:57,394 --> 00:24:00,939
It's some secret
smokers' area that...

437
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:04,735
Kirk went out there at least
six times a day.

438
00:24:06,611 --> 00:24:08,155
Losa must have followed him out.

439
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:12,284
I hate to burst your bubble

440
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:16,037
but Uriel Losa was nowhere
near the convention center

441
00:24:16,163 --> 00:24:18,832
- the day Kirk Upton was killed.
- Seriously?

442
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:22,002
We tracked him.
He was 30 miles away.

443
00:24:22,586 --> 00:24:26,006
He had nothing to do with it.
Still, it was a nice try.

444
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:29,092
"You know, I almost hated to tell him."

445
00:24:29,259 --> 00:24:31,887
- "He had it all worked out."
- Yeah, I know what you mean.

446
00:24:32,053 --> 00:24:34,306
A guilty conscience
is a terrible thing to waste.

447
00:24:34,514 --> 00:24:37,517
In the meantime, we've got nothing
and the gem show ends tonight.

448
00:24:37,768 --> 00:24:39,436
"Well, not completely nothing."

449
00:24:40,103 --> 00:24:41,772
Pond said Upton was a smoker?

450
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:45,066
Well, I think that tells us
who's behind all this.

451
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:48,028
- "Certainly how I can get a confession."
- How?

452
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:51,782
- There is one problem.
- "What?"

453
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:54,659
Well, I'm... I'm a little sick.

454
00:24:54,785 --> 00:24:57,204
I'm not... I'm not sure
that I can do it.

455
00:24:57,454 --> 00:24:59,831
- So what are we gonna do?
- Well, you could do it.

456
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:01,666
- Me?
- Sure.

457
00:25:01,792 --> 00:25:05,128
You've seen me do this
sort of thing heaps of times.

458
00:25:05,670 --> 00:25:09,424
I have no idea what you're gonna say
but I'm pretty sure the answer is no.

459
00:25:09,841 --> 00:25:12,219
Why don't you come by the Airstream
and I'll explain it to you?

460
00:25:12,594 --> 00:25:16,097
- Why can't you just tell me now?
- Because I'd like to see you.

461
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:19,226
"And I was hoping you would
bring me some soup."

462
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:22,687
- Fine.
- Tomato or bean, please.

463
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:23,980
I got it.

464
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:30,237
No, it's... it's cool.
It's like the red badge of courage, only tan.

465
00:25:31,154 --> 00:25:33,448
- The tan badge of courage.
- It's nothing.

466
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,325
Look, you brought the guy in.
That's something.

467
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:36,827
Well, it wasn't enough.

468
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:43,750
Cho will come around.

469
00:25:53,635 --> 00:25:54,845
- Hey, Bob.
- Hey.

470
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,847
- Thanks for coming.
- No problem. What's this all about?

471
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,515
- Let's talk a walk.
- Sure.

472
00:26:04,771 --> 00:26:07,732
You asked if there was
anything in my work

473
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:12,112
with Rio Bravo that could
be problematic. Now...

474
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:16,533
Let's just say,
what if there was?

475
00:26:18,827 --> 00:26:20,787
Well, then that's gonna be
a problem for Lena.

476
00:26:21,037 --> 00:26:23,039
- No, she had nothing to do with it.
- Of course not.

477
00:26:23,456 --> 00:26:25,333
But we need squeaky clean.

478
00:26:26,668 --> 00:26:28,503
If the optics start to look bad

479
00:26:29,462 --> 00:26:31,423
well, we may have to look
for someone else.

480
00:26:33,675 --> 00:26:35,719
Okay. Then what do I need to do?

481
00:26:35,927 --> 00:26:39,139
You know how hard she worked for this, Bob
and I really want her to have this.

482
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,225
All right, look.

483
00:26:43,018 --> 00:26:45,896
As long as you're in the picture
you're potentially an issue.

484
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:50,650
But if you're not a part of the picture
if there's some distance...

485
00:26:50,817 --> 00:26:52,652
What good is that gonna do?
I'm still her husband.

486
00:26:52,861 --> 00:26:55,822
If, for instance, we can put out the word

487
00:26:55,947 --> 00:26:59,868
that you and Lena are going through
a trial separation.

488
00:27:02,871 --> 00:27:05,457
- Are you serious?
- She won't have to say a word.

489
00:27:06,374 --> 00:27:08,251
We just have to make sure
the other side hears it.

490
00:27:09,544 --> 00:27:11,379
It might convince them
to leave you alone.

491
00:27:16,217 --> 00:27:18,178
- No. I can't do that.
- All right.

492
00:27:19,846 --> 00:27:21,765
You want a way to fix it,
and I'm suggesting a way.

493
00:27:25,185 --> 00:27:26,937
Let me know when you decide.

494
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,203
Yes, Lisbon?

495
00:27:44,037 --> 00:27:45,372
So, do you think you can do this?

496
00:27:46,414 --> 00:27:48,208
Jane walked me through it.
I think I can.

497
00:27:49,125 --> 00:27:52,587
She'll have an earphone
and I'll be talking to her all the time.

498
00:27:52,712 --> 00:27:55,924
I'll be able to see everything
that's going on.

499
00:27:56,883 --> 00:27:58,176
She's gonna be fine.

500
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:01,471
And what do you need?

501
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:06,101
I need Wylie to monitor
the security cameras with me.

502
00:28:46,725 --> 00:28:47,767
Hello, Lisbon.

503
00:28:48,601 --> 00:28:50,395
- "Can you hear me?"
- Yes.

504
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:53,732
Well, you look good.
Very convincing.

505
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:56,443
I cannot believe
you talked me into this.

506
00:28:56,776 --> 00:28:59,779
Oh, you're gonna be just fine.
I'm right there with you

507
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:01,698
"inside that head of yours."

508
00:29:01,906 --> 00:29:03,742
- I'm gonna throw up.
- Me, too.

509
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:06,786
Pre-show jitters.
Always get 'em.

510
00:29:14,669 --> 00:29:15,712
Good afternoon.

511
00:29:18,214 --> 00:29:19,257
Little louder.

512
00:29:20,967 --> 00:29:24,554
Good afternoon.
My name is Teresa Lisbon.

513
00:29:25,555 --> 00:29:27,891
- I'm a psychic medium.
- Good.

514
00:29:28,266 --> 00:29:31,019
I work as a special consultant
with the F.B.I.

515
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:35,190
As many of you already know
we're investigating a gem heist

516
00:29:35,356 --> 00:29:37,025
"and the murder of two security guards"

517
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:39,110
along with the murder
of one of your colleagues...

518
00:29:39,486 --> 00:29:40,528
Kirk Upton.

519
00:29:41,196 --> 00:29:45,533
The person behind all this
is in this room right now.

520
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:48,203
Using my gifts

521
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:51,039
I'm gonna reveal
who that person is.

522
00:29:53,416 --> 00:29:54,459
They're hooked.

523
00:29:59,061 --> 00:30:03,691
Yes, I will unmask
Kirk Upton's killer...

524
00:30:06,735 --> 00:30:08,779
very, very soon.

525
00:30:09,113 --> 00:30:10,447
What do you got?
What do you got?

526
00:30:11,682 --> 00:30:12,933
Let's try her.

527
00:30:16,604 --> 00:30:17,855
I got nine hits here.

528
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:20,274
I'm gonna need a little time
before I can get the right one.

529
00:30:20,399 --> 00:30:23,068
Okay. Lisbon, you mind,
stalling for a minute?

530
00:30:27,406 --> 00:30:28,866
Would anybody...

531
00:30:29,450 --> 00:30:32,202
like to ask me a question
before we begin?

532
00:30:33,579 --> 00:30:36,707
Lots of people. You.

533
00:30:37,499 --> 00:30:39,877
There's no such thing
as psychic powers.

534
00:30:41,128 --> 00:30:42,171
Disagree.

535
00:30:43,130 --> 00:30:46,425
- I... I disagree.
- What's my star sign?

536
00:30:46,884 --> 00:30:49,511
Come on, you gotta sell it, Lisbon.
Make 'em believe.

537
00:30:50,387 --> 00:30:56,602
I'm sorry. The spirits won't listen
if there's any negative energy in the room.

538
00:30:59,521 --> 00:31:00,689
Now you're cookin'.

539
00:31:02,149 --> 00:31:03,776
Got her... Mary Kate Barrows.

540
00:31:03,901 --> 00:31:07,112
Okay. Lisbon, you're gonna be
talking to someone called...

541
00:31:08,113 --> 00:31:10,532
Mary Kate Barrows.

542
00:31:10,908 --> 00:31:12,951
"Just like we practiced, okay?"

543
00:31:13,744 --> 00:31:14,995
I'm getting something.

544
00:31:19,667 --> 00:31:22,670
Is there someone named Mary
in this room?

545
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:26,632
- Middle name Kristina or Kathy?
- Kate?

546
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:31,512
Mary Kate. Last name...

547
00:31:31,762 --> 00:31:34,640
your last name,
it's two syllables. It's...

548
00:31:34,848 --> 00:31:38,185
- B-b-b... Barrows.
- Yes.

549
00:31:41,271 --> 00:31:44,608
Mary Kate had a Havanese
called Roger that just died.

550
00:31:44,775 --> 00:31:46,944
- What's a Havanese?
- Oh, my God.

551
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:49,738
Oh, my God.

552
00:31:50,155 --> 00:31:52,908
- It's a little dog.
- It's a dog called Roger.

553
00:31:53,117 --> 00:31:54,284
Oh, my God.

554
00:31:54,952 --> 00:31:57,413
Mary Kate, Roger...

555
00:31:58,038 --> 00:32:01,458
He wants to say hi and that he's okay.

556
00:32:02,835 --> 00:32:05,671
- He can talk?
- Well, yes, of course.

557
00:32:05,963 --> 00:32:10,008
All of God's creatures can talk
in the afterlife.

558
00:32:10,926 --> 00:32:14,096
Move on while you're ahead, Lisbon.
Time to lay the gaff.

559
00:32:16,473 --> 00:32:18,016
I'm getting something else, people.

560
00:32:18,809 --> 00:32:22,479
I'm... I'm hearing another voice right now.
It's a man voice.

561
00:32:22,813 --> 00:32:26,692
Kirk. Kirk? Is that you?

562
00:32:29,862 --> 00:32:30,904
Yes!

563
00:32:32,698 --> 00:32:34,450
"I will speak on your behalf."

564
00:32:35,951 --> 00:32:38,328
Kirk says he was working
with his killer.

565
00:32:38,704 --> 00:32:41,540
They were selling stolen diamonds
for the gem show.

566
00:32:44,501 --> 00:32:45,544
"Kirk?"

567
00:32:46,086 --> 00:32:47,129
Kirk.

568
00:32:47,921 --> 00:32:50,507
Tell us who did this
to you, Kirk.

569
00:32:52,217 --> 00:32:55,053
Wait, Kirk... he wants to speak
directly to his killer.

570
00:32:55,471 --> 00:32:56,972
He says, "Shame on you."

571
00:32:57,890 --> 00:32:59,183
"He thought you were friends."

572
00:32:59,975 --> 00:33:04,271
Everyone's on the edge of their seat.
Keep going, keep going. The smoking bit.

573
00:33:04,605 --> 00:33:08,275
Wait, I-I can't... I can't hear you, Kirk.
You got to speak louder.

574
00:33:10,027 --> 00:33:13,238
Smoking? Wait, wh-what does
smoking have to do with this?

575
00:33:15,282 --> 00:33:18,410
He says, "I hope they have
a lot of nicotine gum in prison."

576
00:33:21,622 --> 00:33:24,124
Tell us, Kirk.
Just give us one name.

577
00:33:26,251 --> 00:33:27,586
He says he'll tell us.

578
00:33:28,587 --> 00:33:31,715
But he wants the killer's mother
to guess first.

579
00:33:32,841 --> 00:33:34,885
He wants the killer to see
the shame in her eyes.

580
00:33:35,093 --> 00:33:38,764
God. Kirk's murder? You?

581
00:33:39,807 --> 00:33:41,225
- Bibby...
- Stay out of it, okay?

582
00:33:41,683 --> 00:33:44,686
You got 'em, Lisbon.
Now close the deal.

583
00:33:47,648 --> 00:33:53,028
If the killer identifies themselves
they'll get a deal with the F.B.I.

584
00:33:53,529 --> 00:33:56,990
If not, I'll find them myself.
No deal.

585
00:33:57,407 --> 00:34:00,160
- Baby, don't be stupid.
- I'm not stupid! Mom!

586
00:34:00,953 --> 00:34:01,995
I'm smart!

587
00:34:02,663 --> 00:34:05,249
And I can do whatever I want
with my life because it's mine!

588
00:34:05,707 --> 00:34:09,962
It's not yours! It's not Kirk's!
It's mine.

589
00:34:10,629 --> 00:34:11,880
Bibby, please!

590
00:34:26,812 --> 00:34:29,398
Kirk and I ran into each other
one night at a bar.

591
00:34:29,940 --> 00:34:31,441
He had just gotten divorced.

592
00:34:32,609 --> 00:34:33,652
We had a few drinks.

593
00:34:34,403 --> 00:34:36,280
One thing led to another.

594
00:34:37,573 --> 00:34:42,077
We realized that we both needed money...
him for his kids, and me...

595
00:34:43,787 --> 00:34:45,163
to get away from my mom.

596
00:34:45,539 --> 00:34:46,832
So we came up with a plan.

597
00:34:47,749 --> 00:34:49,626
I knew when the gems would arrive

598
00:34:49,751 --> 00:34:52,462
from the U.S. buyers that I had
gotten to know over the years

599
00:34:53,463 --> 00:34:56,174
and Kirk knew someone
who could pull off a heist.

600
00:34:57,885 --> 00:34:59,386
"Someone who also needed money."

601
00:35:00,345 --> 00:35:02,347
"A friend from his teenage years."

602
00:35:03,307 --> 00:35:05,642
- "So Elon Bell stole the diamonds."
- Yes.

603
00:35:09,021 --> 00:35:10,772
No one was supposed to die.

604
00:35:12,399 --> 00:35:16,153
When Bell killed those two guards
Kirk freaked out.

605
00:35:17,821 --> 00:35:21,617
But by then, it was...
It was too late.

606
00:35:23,619 --> 00:35:24,745
"Once I got the gems"

607
00:35:26,204 --> 00:35:27,915
"I used my cover
as an appraiser."

608
00:35:28,582 --> 00:35:30,167
"I switched the vendors'
registered gems"

609
00:35:30,292 --> 00:35:33,962
"with the stolen ones, and then I sold
the vendors' gems on the black market."

610
00:35:34,254 --> 00:35:36,298
- And then we showed up.
- Yes.

611
00:35:39,259 --> 00:35:40,761
Kirk wanted to come clean.

612
00:35:42,804 --> 00:35:44,306
And I said he we should
discuss it.

613
00:35:45,766 --> 00:35:47,059
"But there was
no discussing it."

614
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:58,320
Everything I had been holding
inside just came out.

615
00:36:01,156 --> 00:36:02,658
I couldn't stop it.

616
00:36:09,247 --> 00:36:11,124
That woman didn't really
talk to Kirk, did she?

617
00:36:14,419 --> 00:36:15,587
Of course not.

618
00:36:19,174 --> 00:36:21,176
So how did she know I was
chewing nicotine gum?

619
00:36:22,944 --> 00:36:25,113
Mother like yours isn't gonna
let you chew bubble gum.

620
00:36:50,514 --> 00:36:52,849
- You okay?
- Yeah, yeah.

621
00:36:53,683 --> 00:36:54,976
It was just a long day,
that's all.

622
00:36:56,728 --> 00:36:59,022
Well, I've been looking houses
for sale in Georgetown

623
00:36:59,147 --> 00:37:00,607
and they're not as expensive as you think.

624
00:37:00,732 --> 00:37:03,401
I mean, they're expensive,
but they're beautiful houses.

625
00:37:06,780 --> 00:37:07,864
Look, Lena...

626
00:37:10,283 --> 00:37:11,660
I don't think I wanna go to D.C.

627
00:37:13,078 --> 00:37:15,288
You know, I have a good unit
here, seniority

628
00:37:15,413 --> 00:37:16,915
and I don't want to give
those things up.

629
00:37:17,833 --> 00:37:20,919
- What?
- We can be a 2-city couple, right?

630
00:37:21,044 --> 00:37:23,130
- Dennis, stop.
- No, no, no. Other people do it.

631
00:37:23,255 --> 00:37:25,173
- I think it's...
- This is about Rio Bravo, isn't it?

632
00:37:26,174 --> 00:37:27,801
Now I never asked you
what happened down there

633
00:37:27,926 --> 00:37:29,970
and you didn't wanna talk
about it, and I respected that.

634
00:37:30,971 --> 00:37:33,598
But I can't do this anymore,
not if you're acting like this.

635
00:37:34,474 --> 00:37:38,562
- Lena, I can't.
- Baby, it's me. You can tell me anything.

636
00:37:38,687 --> 00:37:40,814
- No, trust me, it needs to be this way.
- Why?

637
00:37:41,148 --> 00:37:42,899
Because you're going to be
asked questions

638
00:37:43,024 --> 00:37:45,652
and if any of those questions
involve Rio Bravo

639
00:37:45,777 --> 00:37:48,613
then you need to be able to say
that you don't know anything about it.

640
00:37:50,866 --> 00:37:52,033
You need that, Lena.

641
00:37:56,955 --> 00:38:00,584
Now, we'll see each other
on weekends and holidays.

642
00:38:03,587 --> 00:38:05,338
You're gonna be working
seven days a week anyway.

643
00:38:05,463 --> 00:38:07,215
It's probably better that I live here.

644
00:38:34,367 --> 00:38:36,286
- Sir, could you please stand up?
- Why?

645
00:38:36,536 --> 00:38:38,163
I'm gonna fall
and I want you to catch me.

646
00:38:38,747 --> 00:38:40,624
- What?
- Then I'll do the same for you.

647
00:38:41,958 --> 00:38:44,252
- No.
- It'll just take a minute.

648
00:38:44,461 --> 00:38:46,171
Vega, you fall right now,
you're gonna hit the floor.

649
00:38:46,463 --> 00:38:48,757
- Well, it's a trust exercise.
- I know what it is.

650
00:38:49,174 --> 00:38:51,009
Well, we did them all the time in training.
They really work.

651
00:38:51,176 --> 00:38:52,802
I'm sure it did in Quantico,
but not here.

652
00:38:53,220 --> 00:38:54,262
Then what do I do?

653
00:38:54,846 --> 00:38:57,224
- I mean, I have to do something.
- Do your job.

654
00:38:58,808 --> 00:39:00,393
- I understand.
- Good.

655
00:39:11,696 --> 00:39:12,739
Vega.

656
00:39:13,406 --> 00:39:16,034
I'm going to the firing range tomorrow
after work. You wanna come along?

657
00:39:16,952 --> 00:39:18,787
- I'd like that.
- Good.

658
00:39:25,043 --> 00:39:27,504
"You need to get some sleep."

659
00:39:31,466 --> 00:39:34,010
You were very good.
Very good.

660
00:39:34,636 --> 00:39:36,680
We were very good.

661
00:39:39,599 --> 00:39:43,937
It was fun, talking to all those people
with you whispering in my ear.

662
00:39:45,188 --> 00:39:46,648
I'd do it again.

663
00:39:51,945 --> 00:39:53,363
What if we just left?

664
00:39:54,948 --> 00:39:55,991
Just took off?

665
00:39:57,534 --> 00:39:58,785
Like, on vacation?

666
00:40:00,912 --> 00:40:01,955
No.

667
00:40:02,956 --> 00:40:03,999
Just leave.

668
00:40:07,335 --> 00:40:09,504
Go someplace different,
move on.

669
00:40:10,297 --> 00:40:12,507
- Well, what do you want to do?
- Oh, I don't know.

670
00:40:14,384 --> 00:40:17,012
But are we really gonna work for the F.B.I.
for the rest of our lives?

671
00:40:17,554 --> 00:40:19,889
Look at dead people,
chase bad guys?

672
00:40:21,683 --> 00:40:24,602
- It's who I am, Jane.
- I know.

673
00:40:26,813 --> 00:40:27,897
Just thoughts.

674
00:40:28,732 --> 00:40:29,774
Just thinking.

675
00:40:32,277 --> 00:40:33,320
Good night.

676
00:40:34,612 --> 00:40:37,198
- I'll come and check on you tomorrow, okay?
- Okay.

677
00:40:38,867 --> 00:40:39,909
Good night.

678
00:40:44,205 --> 00:40:45,248
Sorry.

